special_abilities:
  - name: "The Living Samurai Sword (Daisho)"
    description: "Every true samurai carries a daisho (katana and wakizashi) that are lesser rune weapons, each holding the life essence of a living being. The pair share one alignment and an I.Q. of 3D4+2, and a telepathic bond lets the samurai feel their triumph, courage or fear; they do not speak. Nearly indestructible: the blades never dull and are impervious to magic, demons, elementals and energy; only a god, a Living Legend sword maker or another rune weapon can destroy one. M.D.C.: katana 2D4x100 (ancient pre-Rifts 1800), wakizashi 1D4x100 (ancient 800), regenerating 10 M.D.C. per hour (20 if ancient). Damage: katana 6D6, wakizashi 4D6, as S.D.C. to mortal foes and M.D. to creatures of magic and supernatural beings; ancient blades do 1D6x10 and 1D4x10. If one sword of the pair is lost or destroyed, the other does 1D6 less. The swords give their owner +1 on all saving throws. The samurai can try to parry energy blasts with the sword at -5. Color is always silver, silver-blue or grey. If the swords'' alignment is incompatible with the wielder''s, damage is halved, there is no bonus and the daisho bonuses do not apply; a non-samurai with the heart of a true samurai bonds with them fully. About 25% of samurai and their swords are anarchist or evil. The swords are made only by a samurai of 12th level or higher, a Living Legend Shinto sword maker or an ancient tengu, in a 1000 P.P.E. ritual that binds a human spirit to the blade; the secret gives +9 to resist psionic probes, drugs and mind control that seek it."
  - name: "Way of the Horse and the Bow"
    description: "Samurai Horsemanship: rides any horse-like creature at 54% +4% per level; roll under it for a leap or difficult maneuver such as riding while shooting. Samurai Bowmanship (kyudo), male samurai only: rides and shoots at a full gallop without penalty, and shoots without penalty from a moving vehicle, in mid-air or from an awkward position (other archers lose all strike bonuses and half their rate of fire off balance). Dodges arrows at only -2, energy blasts or gunfire at -4; a dodge uses one melee action. Bow rate of fire: three at level one, +2 at level three, and +1 at levels 4, 6, 9, 12 and 15. Effective range 600 ft (183 m) +25 ft (7.6 m) per level. The female samurai has the horsemanship only."
  - name: "Daisho: The Great and Small"
    description: "Master swordsman trained in Zen and in paired weapons, a sword in each hand striking and parrying at once. Using the katana and wakizashi together as paired weapons: +1 on initiative, +3 to pull punch/sword strike (stop within a centimeter, or deal anything from one point to half damage; a failed roll deals full damage), and one additional attack per melee round."
  - name: "Chi M.D. Death Blow"
    description: "Against oni and demons, dragons, elementals and other supernatural beings and creatures of magic, a punch, kick or hand-held weapon strike inflicts double normal damage plus P.S. bonus as mega-damage, and the victim cannot bio-regenerate that injury for 1D4 hours. Counts as two melee attacks. The samurai must be pure of spirit and intent: never in anger, fear or revenge. Not usable against bots, borgs, power armor, ordinary humans or S.D.C./hit point creatures, and not with guns or the bow. It draws on the character''s P.P.E. and counts as a magical attack."
  - name: "Samurai Fan and the Art of Defense"
    description: "Carries an iron-plated war fan, even into battle, to parry swords and spears in place of a sword or knife. W.P. Iron Fan: +1 to parry at levels 1, 3, 6, 9, 12 and 15. Damage 1D4 S.D.C.; it is not a striking weapon. 30% are mega-damage construction (2D6 M.D.C.). The female samurai''s training list does not include the fan."
restrictions:
  - "Cybernetics: none, for any reason. Only 10% will even consider bio-systems."
  - "Hand to Hand: Zanji Shinjinken-Ryo (males) or Kendo (females); no combat alternatives."
  - "Lives by the Bushido code of the New Empire; avoids technology."
side_effects: "Money: 3D4 x 1000 credits is a personal savings in gold, gems and other valuables. The daimyo supplies clothing, food, shelter, horse, arrows and common S.D.C. weapons and armor, and family holdings pay a monthly wage of about 1D4 x 1000 credits. Of all booty, 20% goes to the local daimyo or shogunate, 20% to the Empire and 20% to the family holdings. A samurai of 12th level or higher can make true samurai swords."
extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 8: Japan printed 43-49 (cache p044-p050, a text layer, page_offset +1). The entry opens under Traditional Samurai Warrior O.C.C. on printed 43; printed 45 (cache p046) is a full-page illustration, rendered; the stat block starts on printed 48 and its Money paragraph continues onto printed 49, which also holds Female Samurai. Printed 49 then opens the Ronin O.C.C. || XP: the Ronin, True Samurai column on printed 216 (cache p217), read off a render: 0 / 2,151 / 4,301 / 8,601 / 17,201 / 25,501 / 36,001 / 52,001 / 73,001 / 98,001 / 134,001 / 184,001 / 240,001 / 295,001 / 385,001. || GROUP: men-of-arms, men_of_arms: true, from the section heading Warrior & Monk O.C.C.s and the entry heading Traditional Samurai Warrior O.C.C.; no O.C.C. S.D.C. is printed (Zanji and Kendo add theirs on the skill rows). || VARIANTS: male and female. The male takes Hand to Hand: Zanji Shinjinken-Ryo and W.P. Samurai Archery (stored as Rifts Japan''s W.P. Bow); the Female Samurai (printed 49) takes Kendo and W.P. Spear instead, does not use the bow, keeps W.P. Sword, paired weapons and the daisho, and has P.P.E. of P.E. x3 +1D6 per level where the male has P.E. x2 +1D6 per level. Everything else is the male''s. A variant cannot change equipment or abilities, so the bow stays in the shared kit with a note and the female''s narrower Special Training (horsemanship only, no fan) is prose. || HAND TO HAND: No combat alternatives are allowed, so costs: {}. The style bonuses live on the skill rows and are not repeated here. || SKILLS: Climbing 40+5, Horsemanship +20 on Horsemanship: General (40+20=60; the Special Training prints Samurai Horsemanship at 54% +4%, kept in the note and the ability), Demon & Monster Lore is Lore: Demons & Monsters 25+15, Wilderness Survival 30+10, Tracking is Tracking (people) 25+5, Go 30+10, Calligraphy 35+10, Literacy: Japanese is Literacy: Native Language 40+15, Japanese at 98% is Language: Native Tongue, two languages +10% as two Language: Other picks, Mathematics: Basic 45+15. Paired Weapons is granted from the daisho training (Special Training #2), which the skill list refers to. W.P. two of choice: no limit printed. || BACKGROUND: the Samurai Family Background table (printed 47-48) is a d100 roll naming which categories the three +10% background skills come from; the table is prose in the body and the picks are one choose-3 group over the union of those categories, with the roll''s limit shown in the note. The Noble result''s older, greater-weapon daisho is prose. || RELATED: four, plus one at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12. Communications none except literacy, which the book files under Technical and the catalog under Communications, so Communications is granted with literacy only at the Technical +10%. Technical art, literacy, language, lores and writing only: the named catalog rows; Mythology and Japanese Mythology are not lore by the book''s own split (printed 48 lists lore and mythology separately) and are left out. W.P. any ancient: the catalog''s ancient-weapon W.P. rows, chosen by hand. Science: Astronomy and Mathematics. Rogue: background only. || SECONDARY: the book prints two secondary skills at levels two, six and ten, read as none at level one and two at each of those levels. || BONUSES: +1 save vs horror factor at levels 1, 4, 6, 8, 10 and 12, and +1 vs mind control. The swords'' +1 on all saves and the daisho bonuses depend on the swords and are prose. || MONEY: 3D4 x 1000 credits of personal savings in gold, gems and valuables, stored as starting money; the monthly 1D4 x 1000 wage is prose. || EQUIPMENT: the Living Samurai Sword (printed 44-46) is a lesser rune daisho with its own stats and no catalog row of its own. daisho-rifts, the mundane pair, is granted as the item with a note, and the rune features and stats are the Living Samurai Sword ability (the same shape as the Ronin draft). The magic samurai armor (samurai-armor) and silver-tipped arrows (silver-tipped-arrows) had no catalog rows; both slugs are shared with the Ronin. Two weapons of choice as weapons-matching-w-p-skills."
